<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21338] Check lock limit for resent lock requests</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21338</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;check lock limit for resent lock requests&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    The server only enforced ldlm.lock_limit_mb on first-time enqueues,&lt;br/&gt;
    so a client rejected with -EINPROGRESS simply got its lock a second&lt;br/&gt;
    later when it resent with MSG_RESENT (letting the lock count grow&lt;br/&gt;
    far past the limit), and the fix applies the limit check to resent&lt;br/&gt;
    enqueues too, unless they already have a lock on the export, are&lt;br/&gt;
    replays, have a saved reply, or are of an uncounted lock type&lt;br/&gt;
    (FLOCK/PLAIN).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    In after_reply(), each -EINPROGRESS reply makes the client schedule&lt;br/&gt;
    a resend after a delay that grows by one second per rejection (1s,&lt;br/&gt;
    2s, 3s, ...), capped at the request timeout and retried&lt;br/&gt;
    indefinitely; ptl_send_rpc() then sends it with a new XID and&lt;br/&gt;
    MSG_RESENT.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
